# CTT: dhclient ENTER hook for the Telit CDC-ECM data interface (mdm0).
#
# Sourced by /sbin/dhclient-script BEFORE it configures the interface, so the
# variables set here change what it does. Scoped by $interface, so every other
# dhclient invocation is untouched — in practice there are none: NetworkManager
# uses its own internal DHCP client for eth0/wlan0, and dhcpcd5 is installed by
# the Pi image but disabled.
#
# new_dhcp_lease_time=""
#   dhclient-script applies the kernel address lifetime as
#   ${new_dhcp_lease_time:+valid_lft $new_dhcp_lease_time}, on BOTH of its paths:
#   `ip -4 addr add` (BOUND/REBOOT) and `ip -4 addr change` (RENEW/REBIND).
#   Blanking it installs the address PERMANENT rather than DYNAMIC.
#
#   Why: the LE910Q1's built-in DHCP server issues an 86400 s lease, and nothing
#   renews it. ctt-modem-ecm-up.service is a Type=oneshot with RemainAfterExit=no,
#   so the daemonized dhclient is reaped with the unit's cgroup as soon as
#   ExecStart returns (deliberately — a renewer that outlives a USB re-enumeration
#   cannot re-lease on the new netdev and just loops "send_packet: Network is
#   unreachable"; 13,703 such lines on V30B0154C65F, 2026-08-27). The kernel
#   therefore deleted mdm0's address exactly 24 h after every boot. With no
#   non-loopback IPv4 left, glibc's AI_ADDRCONFIG stops returning 127.0.0.1 for
#   `localhost`, so every internal client resolves ::1 alone and gets
#   ECONNREFUSED against station-hardware-server (which binds 127.0.0.1 only);
#   station-radio-interface exits on an unhandled rejection and crash-loops, and
#   data collection stops. Observed on 6CA25D375881: address withdrawn
#   2026-10-04 06:43:35, 24 h after the 10-03 boot, first ECONNREFUSED 31 s later.
#
# IF_METRIC=700
#   dhclient-script installs the default route as
#   `ip -4 route add default via $router dev $interface ${if_metric:+metric ...}`,
#   taking if_metric from IF_METRIC — and it reads that AFTER sourcing this hook.
#   Setting it here creates the route at the fallback metric directly, so the
#   metric-0 route that would outrank eth0 (~50) and wlan0 (~600) and silently
#   capture all station traffic never exists. 700 is above eth0 (~50) and wlan0
#   (~600), so cellular is used only when no wired/WiFi default has a route.
case "$interface" in
  mdm0)
    new_dhcp_lease_time=""
    IF_METRIC=700
    ;;
esac
